    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "I don't specifically care. For historical reasons unknown to me `cuml` has hypothesis tests that sometimes run with byteswapped arrays, and I ran into what I viewed as weird behavior here with `cupy` being inconsistent with `numpy`. FWIW I view all of this as edge case handling and unlikely to be hit by real user code.\n\nErroring when doing something different than numpy might be nicer than silently doing a different thing here? I'm not really sure what the best option is, mostly opened this to point out the difference.",
